WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.006
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.276 --> 00:07.695
There's a spy in Gate 24?

3
00:07.779 --> 00:10.240
Ever since the regime change two years ago in Astoria,

4
00:10.323 --> 00:11.950
an anti-government organization

5
00:12.033 --> 00:15.829
called Wings of the People has been committing frequent acts of terror.

6
00:15.912 --> 00:19.082
They suspect it was caused by Wings of the People.

7
00:19.165 --> 00:21.334
If anything, we should suspect the government.

8
00:21.960 --> 00:24.963
A man suspected of involvement in the government facility bombing

9
00:25.046 --> 00:25.964
six months ago

10
00:26.047 --> 00:27.966
boarded the flight from Astoria.

11
00:28.049 --> 00:30.885
I have nothing to say.

12
00:30.969 --> 00:32.887
What did you just swallow?

13
00:32.971 --> 00:35.223
Hey!

14
00:35.306 --> 00:37.934
Why would Shirosaki be in an anti-government group?

15
00:38.017 --> 00:40.895
Actually, we found this among Kazuo Shirosaki's

16
00:40.979 --> 00:43.106
personal belongings.

17
00:43.189 --> 00:45.483
The counselor's business card?

18
00:45.567 --> 00:51.573
You are suspected of having ties to an anti-government organization.

19
00:53.700 --> 00:58.121
Counselor Sugihara, you have stayed in Astoria in the past, haven't you?

20
00:58.746 --> 01:02.083
-Wait a minute-- -How did a member of Wings of the People

21
01:02.167 --> 01:04.043
come to possess this business card?

22
01:04.961 --> 01:06.462
-Well, that's-- -Let's go.

23
01:15.263 --> 01:16.598
Fine.

24
01:17.223 --> 01:18.141
Let's go.

25
01:24.564 --> 01:26.357
Airport Director, what's going on?

26
01:26.441 --> 01:28.735
-This must be some kind of mistake, right? -But

27
01:28.818 --> 01:30.695
how do we explain that business card?

28
01:30.778 --> 01:33.740
That could be a fake, couldn't it?

29
01:39.412 --> 01:41.581
Is that the counselor's business card?

30
01:42.790 --> 01:44.083
It is.

31
01:44.167 --> 01:46.544
It's exactly like the one we just saw.

32
01:47.170 --> 01:48.129
So it's genuine?

33
01:48.796 --> 01:50.131
Why do you have that card?

34
01:53.843 --> 01:54.677
Mori?

35
01:57.722 --> 02:02.352
In any case, Counselor Sugihara is currently under serious suspicion.

36
02:02.435 --> 02:05.438
Which means, the survival of the gate

37
02:05.521 --> 02:07.607
-also hangs on this. -Wait a second.

38
02:07.690 --> 02:09.442
You're going to get rid of Gate 24?

39
02:09.525 --> 02:11.277
Depending on what the questioning reveals.

40
02:16.616 --> 02:17.867
Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa.

41
02:18.910 --> 02:22.997
Until then, I'll leave the operations of this gate in your hands.

42
02:39.639 --> 02:41.391
Counselor Sugihara!

43
02:46.521 --> 02:49.023
MIDORI SUGIHARA

44
03:01.786 --> 03:02.662
Are you okay?

45
03:12.964 --> 03:14.674
The counselor…

46
03:17.969 --> 03:20.972
is in a gray area right now.

47
03:24.058 --> 03:26.060
If we find out exactly where in the gray zone she is,

48
03:26.769 --> 03:28.896
we should be able to find out the truth.

49
03:31.315 --> 03:32.275
But…

50
03:38.448 --> 03:39.407
I'm scared.

51
03:41.826 --> 03:42.869
Until now,

52
03:44.245 --> 03:49.292
I always hated

53
03:52.128 --> 03:53.296
leaving something unexplained.

54
03:55.298 --> 03:56.257
But…

55
03:57.925 --> 03:58.968
now…

56
04:04.974 --> 04:06.642
I'm afraid…

57
04:09.187 --> 04:10.563
of finding out the truth.

58
04:36.005 --> 04:37.632
CHIKA KUMAGAWA - GROUND STAFF

59
04:37.715 --> 04:38.800
Chika…

60
04:41.260 --> 04:42.553
That's unusual.

61
04:44.180 --> 04:45.181
You, slacking off work?

62
04:48.059 --> 04:50.686
It seems Mori is taking the day off.

63
04:50.770 --> 04:51.729
AKIHIKO SEIKE - IMMIGRATION OFFICIAL

64
04:52.647 --> 04:57.235
I see. She must really be shaken up about the counselor.

65
04:57.318 --> 05:00.488
Mori really respected her.

66
05:00.571 --> 05:01.489
But

67
05:01.572 --> 05:05.243
if the Counselor really is involved with an anti-government organization…

68
05:05.326 --> 05:07.453
-What are you saying? -No, hypothetically!

69
05:07.537 --> 05:09.414
We don't need hypotheticals right now!

70
05:10.289 --> 05:11.416
Sorry.

71
05:14.377 --> 05:15.503
Chief.

72
05:16.087 --> 05:17.588
What's happening with the counselor?

73
05:18.464 --> 05:20.508
She's still being questioned.

74
05:20.591 --> 05:24.345
But if we let ourselves get rattled,

75
05:24.429 --> 05:26.139
we won't be able to inspect carefully.

76
05:26.931 --> 05:28.933
For now, let's focus on the work in front of us.

77
05:29.684 --> 05:30.977
-Yes, sir. -Yes, sir.

78
05:31.060 --> 05:33.896
Besides, today is especially important.

79
05:33.980 --> 05:37.650
Yes. This afternoon, Astorian President Alberto Roden

80
05:37.733 --> 05:39.986
is coming to Japan for a summit meeting.

81
06:01.799 --> 06:03.718
The place is on high alert, huh?

82
06:03.801 --> 06:06.220
According to the police, the leader of Wings of the People

83
06:06.304 --> 06:08.222
is entering Japan soon.

84
06:08.306 --> 06:09.557
The leader?

85
06:09.640 --> 06:11.893
They may also be bringing in funds for their activities.

86
06:11.976 --> 06:13.436
That's not all.

87
06:13.519 --> 06:16.439
We also have information that Wings of the People

88
06:16.522 --> 06:19.525
is planning to assassinate the Astorian president.

89
06:19.609 --> 06:23.404
Then is that also why Shirosaki came to Japan?

90
06:23.487 --> 06:27.325
But once his identity was exposed, he feared the plan would be leaked.

91
06:27.408 --> 06:30.244
So he took his own life to guard it?

92
06:30.328 --> 06:32.830
What we need to do doesn't change.

93
06:32.914 --> 06:37.251
As always, carefully inspect who and what is coming through.

94
06:37.793 --> 06:38.961
-Yes, sir. -Yes, sir.

95
06:40.838 --> 06:45.635
It's true that I went to Astoria three years ago

96
06:45.718 --> 06:50.431
as part of a government delegation. But I was only there for about a week,

97
06:50.514 --> 06:53.476
and I never met Shirosaki while I was there.

98
06:54.352 --> 06:55.728
Have you ever met him before?

99
06:57.146 --> 06:58.481
Only once.

100
07:00.441 --> 07:02.276
When? Where?

101
07:03.444 --> 07:07.865
At a reception held by an international medical organization four years ago.

102
07:07.949 --> 07:08.783
MIDORI SUGIHARA

103
07:08.866 --> 07:10.409
-Even then, -I'm Sugihara.

104
07:10.493 --> 07:12.537
-I just gave him my business card. -I'm Shirosaki.

105
07:12.620 --> 07:15.248
We didn't really have a conversation, and

106
07:15.873 --> 07:17.959
-I haven't met him since. -I see.

107
07:18.042 --> 07:19.627
That would explain it.

108
07:19.710 --> 07:20.962
Wait.

109
07:21.546 --> 07:23.130
She could have been lying, you know.

110
07:24.924 --> 07:27.343
You could have actually met Shirosaki in Astoria

111
07:27.426 --> 07:29.971
and given him this card then.

112
07:30.555 --> 07:33.140
-That's not true. -Then you'll have to prove it.

113
07:36.143 --> 07:38.938
I see. The counselor, huh…

114
07:45.111 --> 07:46.112
What's that?

115
07:46.821 --> 07:47.822
I got it

116
07:47.905 --> 07:51.075
from the Counselor a long time ago when I was working

117
07:51.701 --> 07:53.744
at a museum in Astoria.

118
07:53.828 --> 07:54.954
In Astoria?

119
07:55.830 --> 07:58.040
Well, she didn't really give it to me.

120
07:58.874 --> 08:01.544
I sort of of just picked it up.

121
08:03.045 --> 08:07.300
So then she told me…

122
08:07.883 --> 08:09.176
What'd she tell you?

123
08:10.469 --> 08:11.387
That someday…

124
08:11.470 --> 08:14.599
I will make the best gate in the world, to protect the country.

125
08:17.393 --> 08:19.186
So that's why you became a customs official?

126
08:20.313 --> 08:22.231
That's some serious determination.

127
08:26.277 --> 08:28.904
Objects don't lie.

128
08:31.032 --> 08:33.743
I've always believed that.

129
08:35.953 --> 08:37.079
But…

130
08:39.498 --> 08:42.460
If it's bothering you that much, why don't you just throw it away?

131
08:43.836 --> 08:46.339
If you carry this around, you'll keep dwelling on it forever.

132
08:49.467 --> 08:51.010
Oh my.

133
08:52.219 --> 08:53.262
What…

134
08:55.014 --> 08:55.973
It was my business card.

135
08:58.309 --> 08:59.310
Look.

136
09:00.061 --> 09:02.021
I'd never do something like that.

137
09:04.815 --> 09:07.693
You just have to do what you can, right?

138
09:11.238 --> 09:12.323
MIDORI SUGIHARA

139
09:12.406 --> 09:13.407
Machi.

140
09:17.036 --> 09:18.996
Some important foreigner is coming today, right?

141
09:19.955 --> 09:21.374
Are you two on security duty?

142
09:21.457 --> 09:23.834
No, we're continuing the investigation.

143
09:24.710 --> 09:28.130
I never thought someone at the Counselor level would get involved…

144
09:28.214 --> 09:29.340
Iuchi!

145
09:29.423 --> 09:31.300
-Huh? -Machi.

146
09:32.968 --> 09:35.179
What's up? What is it?

147
09:36.138 --> 09:37.431
I need a favor.

148
09:38.307 --> 09:40.518
PREPARING TO OPEN

149
09:43.604 --> 09:45.147
Wait, are you sure this is okay?

150
09:45.231 --> 09:48.150
It is if I say so!

151
09:50.486 --> 09:52.321
This is the business card we're concerned about.

152
09:52.405 --> 09:53.948
-Iuchi! -Shut up.

153
09:54.990 --> 09:57.993
If it gives us a lead, that's part of a proper investigation.

154
10:02.415 --> 10:03.666
Thank you very much.

155
10:04.709 --> 10:06.877
MIDORI SUGIHARA

156
10:15.302 --> 10:16.470
Oh my.

157
10:17.888 --> 10:19.098
The question is

158
10:20.766 --> 10:25.020
whether you actually had a connection with Wings of the People.

159
10:25.104 --> 10:27.565
You gave this to him in Astoria, didn't you?

160
10:28.149 --> 10:30.317
Why don't you just tell us the truth?

161
10:37.283 --> 10:39.452
-Excuse me. -Iuchi!

162
10:39.994 --> 10:42.538
I'm Iuchi, from the Tokyo Metropolitan Police Department.

163
10:42.621 --> 10:44.373
May I have a moment?

164
10:44.457 --> 10:45.374
Go ahead.

165
10:46.292 --> 10:49.837
Actually, I brought someone with me. Hey.

166
10:54.341 --> 10:55.176
Mori.

167
10:56.260 --> 10:57.636
Who is that?

168
10:58.220 --> 11:00.973
She says she found out something about this case.

169
11:01.557 --> 11:03.392
-She found something? -Yes.

170
11:04.477 --> 11:08.105
Counselor Sugihara did not give that business card to Shirosaki

171
11:08.189 --> 11:09.482
in Astoria.

172
11:10.149 --> 11:11.233
What are you talking about?

173
11:12.026 --> 11:13.903
-There's no way you could know that. -I do.

174
11:14.987 --> 11:20.159
All right. This is the business card found in Shirosaki's possession.

175
11:25.831 --> 11:26.999
Thank you.

176
11:27.666 --> 11:30.878
This card is 55 by 91 millimeters.

177
11:30.961 --> 11:33.714
That's the standard size used in Japan.

178
11:33.797 --> 11:37.510
But business card sizes vary by country and region.

179
11:37.593 --> 11:39.678
The business cards the counselor used in Astoria

180
11:39.762 --> 11:43.015
were 55 by 85 millimeters, the European size, correct?

181
11:43.599 --> 11:48.229
Yes. I use different business cards in Japan and overseas.

182
11:48.312 --> 11:53.234
Then the card Shirosaki had was a domestic Japanese business card?

183
11:54.026 --> 11:55.277
Yes.

184
11:55.361 --> 11:56.362
Wait a second!

185
11:56.987 --> 12:00.908
You don't know whether the counselor actually used that size in Astoria.

186
12:03.244 --> 12:04.578
Thank you.

187
12:06.539 --> 12:07.748
-Here. -Thank you very much.

188
12:09.333 --> 12:11.085
-Here, here. -Thank you.

189
12:13.879 --> 12:17.132
I was working in Astoria at the time too.

190
12:17.216 --> 12:21.136
This is the business card the Counselor was using then.

191
12:30.521 --> 12:32.940
MIDORI SUGIHARA

192
12:34.358 --> 12:36.860
They really are different.

193
12:36.944 --> 12:38.737
This is proof.

194
12:44.243 --> 12:45.369
I see.

195
12:47.329 --> 12:48.330
I understand.

196
12:49.623 --> 12:51.458
However, this doesn't prove

197
12:51.542 --> 12:55.379
that the counselor is not connected to Wings of the People.

198
12:56.630 --> 12:57.464
Correct.

199
12:57.548 --> 13:01.176
We'll have the Public Security Bureau verify that.

200
13:05.264 --> 13:08.934
W-w-ait!

201
13:11.353 --> 13:16.734
T-then please tell the Public Security Bureau this.

202
13:17.443 --> 13:24.283
Counselor Sugihara is a truly, truly incredible person.

203
13:26.243 --> 13:29.121
The reason the counselor established Gate 24

204
13:29.204 --> 13:31.123
was to protect this country.

205
13:31.206 --> 13:35.336
She worked tirelessly to tear down the barriers between government agencies.

206
13:35.419 --> 13:36.503
Mori.

207
13:36.587 --> 13:39.340
No matter what happened, she always stood in front of us

208
13:39.423 --> 13:42.176
and said she'd take responsibility.

209
13:42.259 --> 13:46.597
Even when I caused one problem after another, she never abandoned me.

210
13:46.680 --> 13:47.765
Mori.

211
13:48.849 --> 13:50.559
-And-- -There's still more?

212
13:50.643 --> 13:52.936
-Let's go. -Mori!

213
13:54.438 --> 13:55.814
That's enough.

214
13:56.857 --> 13:59.693
More importantly, what about your work?

215
14:02.696 --> 14:03.697
Well…

216
14:03.781 --> 14:04.948
I'll be fine.

217
14:06.241 --> 14:09.370
Go do what you need to do.

218
14:10.871 --> 14:11.789
Yes!

219
14:13.040 --> 14:14.208
Excuse me.

220
14:15.918 --> 14:19.421
Hey, hey, hey! T-take your…

221
14:19.505 --> 14:20.839
Take your bag.

222
14:30.724 --> 14:33.727
The flight from Vuldinia will be arriving shortly.

223
14:33.811 --> 14:34.728
Yes.

224
14:40.317 --> 14:43.988
Actually, Tsumugi is on this flight.

225
14:44.071 --> 14:45.489
-Huh? -What?

226
14:45.572 --> 14:47.908
-Tsumugi's coming home today? -Yes.

227
14:48.492 --> 14:49.743
Her mother is here to pick her up.

228
14:50.369 --> 14:52.037
So you three can spend time together.

229
14:52.121 --> 14:53.914
Actually,

230
14:53.998 --> 14:57.042
she's coming to Japan with a friend she made while studying abroad.

231
14:57.126 --> 14:59.169
That's nice, coming back with a friend.

232
14:59.253 --> 15:01.255
Are you sure that's not her boyfriend?

233
15:01.922 --> 15:03.048
-Hey, hey… -Sorry.

234
15:04.091 --> 15:05.175
‎-Seike, you know, ‎-Yes?

235
15:05.843 --> 15:09.221
everyone's trying to stay cheerful despite what's going on.

236
15:10.764 --> 15:14.351
We don't know what'll happen to this place. Mori isn't here,

237
15:14.435 --> 15:16.103
and you're looking gloomy too.

238
15:16.812 --> 15:17.980
No.

239
15:18.063 --> 15:20.065
Come on. Smile, smile.

240
15:23.027 --> 15:25.029
-You're the boyfriend? -Matsuyama.

241
15:26.155 --> 15:27.406
-I didn't say it! -No, no!

242
15:27.489 --> 15:29.241
But I won't tell.

243
15:29.324 --> 15:31.452
-That's great, isn't it? Isn't it? -Wait!

244
15:32.536 --> 15:34.371
Please take care of his daughter.

245
15:35.497 --> 15:37.708
-Stop! -I'm just kidding!

246
15:37.791 --> 15:38.792
Mori?

247
15:39.626 --> 15:41.253
Aren't you taking the day off?

248
15:42.504 --> 15:44.131
Sorry I'm late.

249
15:47.926 --> 15:49.636
-Let's go. -Yes.

250
15:51.472 --> 15:55.517
-They're arriving. Let's go, go, go. -Yes, sir!

251
16:16.371 --> 16:17.873
Please have your passport ready.

252
16:18.415 --> 16:20.918
Mori! I'm back.

253
16:21.001 --> 16:23.295
Tsumugi, welcome home. Go ahead.

254
16:23.378 --> 16:24.338
Okay.

255
16:25.130 --> 16:26.757
-Noa, I'll go ahead. -Okay.

256
16:28.425 --> 16:29.927
-Passport, please. -Here.

257
16:31.220 --> 16:32.387
‎Here.

258
16:32.471 --> 16:34.848
-Okay, Tsumugi Fukazawa, right? -Yes.

259
16:37.476 --> 16:38.685
PERMISSION TO ENTER

260
16:38.769 --> 16:41.522
-Welcome home. -Thank you very much.

261
16:42.523 --> 16:43.607
Welcome home.

262
16:44.233 --> 16:47.361
Don't we have to check her luggage?

263
16:47.444 --> 16:49.571
She's the chief's daughter.

264
16:51.698 --> 16:52.783
Dad!

265
16:58.330 --> 16:59.331
Huh?

266
17:00.249 --> 17:01.667
He's working.

267
17:02.376 --> 17:03.460
You're right.

268
17:04.253 --> 17:08.257
Oh, right. This is my friend Noa. We met in London.

269
17:08.799 --> 17:10.968
We also volunteered together. Right?

270
17:11.051 --> 17:14.805
We went to Vuldinia together and then came straight to Japan.

271
17:14.888 --> 17:16.431
-I'll wait over there. -Okay.

272
17:37.703 --> 17:39.663
My father is Japanese.

273
17:39.746 --> 17:41.582
But this is my first time coming to Japan.

274
17:41.665 --> 17:43.250
I've been looking forward to it.

275
17:43.333 --> 17:45.544
I see. Well then.

276
17:45.627 --> 17:48.088
I'll check your luggage over here.

277
18:20.078 --> 18:22.039
GUSTAVE KRONE

278
18:45.646 --> 18:47.397
Find some place I like

279
18:48.190 --> 18:49.024
and just take it easy.

280
18:50.943 --> 18:52.069
I see.

281
18:57.032 --> 18:57.991
Could you come with us?

282
18:58.075 --> 18:59.284
Is there a problem?

283
18:59.368 --> 19:01.411
It's just a formality.

284
19:02.996 --> 19:04.331
I'll take your suitcase.

285
19:06.083 --> 19:07.209
Right this way.

286
19:33.402 --> 19:35.821
What's this?

287
19:36.697 --> 19:40.409
The children I volunteered with gave me this sachet as a present.

288
19:40.951 --> 19:42.577
Are these herbs?

289
19:43.161 --> 19:45.747
-There are seeds too. -You're right.

290
19:46.581 --> 19:49.376
Did Tsumugi receive one too, by any chance?

291
19:49.459 --> 19:50.294
Yes.

292
19:52.671 --> 19:53.672
Tsumugi.

293
19:54.715 --> 19:57.384
I'm sorry. May I check your luggage?

294
19:58.260 --> 19:59.219
Yes.

295
19:59.303 --> 20:02.055
-We… -Is there a problem?

296
20:02.139 --> 20:05.183
These need to be checked by plant quarantine.

297
20:05.267 --> 20:07.769
-Utsuki, please. -Coming.

298
20:12.190 --> 20:14.443
How long will it take?

299
20:14.526 --> 20:15.902
It depends on the type,

300
20:15.986 --> 20:17.446
so I can't say yet.

301
20:17.529 --> 20:19.948
We'll need to examine them more thoroughly in another room.

302
20:20.032 --> 20:20.949
Okay.

303
20:25.245 --> 20:26.330
Emergency alert.

304
20:30.208 --> 20:31.543
Emergency alert.

305
20:31.626 --> 20:34.713
An explosion has been confirmed in the north lobby.

306
20:34.796 --> 20:38.091
The cause is a power bank catching fire. No injuries.

307
20:40.510 --> 20:43.221
-A power bank? -We need to be careful too.

308
20:44.306 --> 20:47.267
Looks like Tsumugi got one of those presents too.

309
20:47.351 --> 20:49.436
Mori, I'll leave the two of them with you.

310
20:49.519 --> 20:50.771
-Understood. -Right this way.

311
20:51.480 --> 20:52.606
-Thank you. -Thank you.

312
20:52.689 --> 20:54.733
-I'll carry your luggage. -Okay.

313
20:54.816 --> 20:56.318
Everything looks okay for now.

314
20:56.985 --> 20:57.861
Yes.

315
20:58.904 --> 21:02.324
Hayami. Let that passenger through.

316
21:05.077 --> 21:06.703
Forget the inspection.

317
21:08.080 --> 21:09.498
Let him enter the country.

318
21:23.095 --> 21:24.679
I'll help with your luggage.

319
21:24.763 --> 21:25.680
Okay.

320
21:29.851 --> 21:31.103
Excuse me.

321
21:37.818 --> 21:39.611
-Please. -Okay.

322
21:43.115 --> 21:45.409
You two have matching suitcases.

323
21:45.951 --> 21:48.495
Yes. Noa gave it to me.

324
21:49.788 --> 21:53.291
Tsumugi helped me so much with volunteering,

325
21:53.375 --> 21:54.501
so it was a thank-you gift.

326
21:54.584 --> 21:57.587
-You two are close. -Yes!

327
21:57.671 --> 22:00.298
We wanted to get the same scarves too.

328
22:00.382 --> 22:03.427
If we got the same one, we wouldn't know whose is whose.

329
22:04.094 --> 22:05.846
It's a nice pattern.

330
22:05.929 --> 22:07.681
I've always loved it.

331
22:09.433 --> 22:11.518
Where did I pack it?

332
22:12.102 --> 22:13.395
Noa, you don't have it?

333
22:14.104 --> 22:15.480
What?

334
22:15.564 --> 22:17.983
May I check yours as well, to be safe?

335
22:18.066 --> 22:19.109
Yes.

336
22:19.693 --> 22:20.986
Excuse me.

337
22:30.996 --> 22:31.997
-Please. -Okay.

338
22:44.926 --> 22:48.180
Your items are similar too.

339
22:51.892 --> 22:54.603
We shop together a lot.

340
22:54.686 --> 22:56.229
And our tastes always match.

341
23:04.362 --> 23:06.740
Found it! This is it.

342
23:06.823 --> 23:07.782
Just here.

343
23:07.866 --> 23:08.742
Okay.

344
23:09.701 --> 23:13.163
I'll check whether these seeds are permitted to enter Japan.

345
23:13.246 --> 23:15.498
-Please wait a moment. -Okay.

346
23:23.465 --> 23:25.550
Chief, what's going on?

347
23:27.427 --> 23:30.430
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs made a request.

348
23:30.513 --> 23:36.019
We were told to let all the passengers here through before the president arrives.

349
23:36.102 --> 23:37.354
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs?

350
23:38.230 --> 23:40.357
They said it's a security measure.

351
23:40.440 --> 23:43.068
But that man Krone is suspicious.

352
23:43.151 --> 23:46.071
-We need to inspect him more thoroughly. -Just let him through.

353
23:47.530 --> 23:49.574
Do you not trust my judgment?

354
23:50.158 --> 23:51.243
Well…

355
23:55.497 --> 23:57.707
Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa.

356
23:58.291 --> 23:59.709
About Tsumugi's luggage…

357
23:59.793 --> 24:02.212
If there's a problem, deal with it quickly and let her through.

358
24:04.005 --> 24:08.301
Get all the passengers here through the gate as quickly as possible.

359
24:25.860 --> 24:27.320
Chief…

360
24:27.404 --> 24:28.738
Did you not hear me?

361
24:32.367 --> 24:34.494
Yes, I understand.

362
24:36.538 --> 24:40.625
Hayami, Matsuyama, could I speak with you for a moment?

363
24:48.675 --> 24:51.261
-Excuse us for a moment. -Okay.

364
25:00.312 --> 25:02.564
That signal just now meant there's someone suspicious.

365
25:02.647 --> 25:03.481
Don't tell me you mean…

366
25:03.565 --> 25:05.692
Yes. Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa.

367
25:06.359 --> 25:07.736
I was suspicious too.

368
25:07.819 --> 25:09.821
The chief's been acting strange today.

369
25:09.904 --> 25:11.698
He told me to let a suspicious passenger through.

370
25:11.781 --> 25:13.658
Even if it were a request from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs,

371
25:13.742 --> 25:16.411
he wouldn't normally order us to neglect an inspection.

372
25:16.494 --> 25:18.204
What did you notice, Mori?

373
25:19.497 --> 25:20.623
Um…

374
25:21.708 --> 25:24.878
Where is Chief Fukazawa's wife right now?

375
25:25.587 --> 25:27.339
-Huh? -Why are you asking that?

376
25:27.422 --> 25:31.718
There were three things about the chief that bothered me.

377
25:32.260 --> 25:36.514
First, he started closing the blinds in the room.

378
25:37.182 --> 25:39.017
That bothered me as well.

379
25:39.100 --> 25:40.769
He can't see the booths like that.

380
25:41.770 --> 25:43.396
Second, the sound of his shoes.

381
25:44.481 --> 25:45.982
The sound of his shoes?

382
25:46.066 --> 25:48.068
It was always at the same interval.

383
25:48.151 --> 25:50.737
It's the Alpine Distress Signal.

384
25:50.820 --> 25:53.698
The signal used to call for help when someone is stranded in the mountains.

385
25:54.532 --> 25:56.409
One sound every ten seconds.

386
25:56.493 --> 26:01.664
Six times in one minute, followed by one minute of silence.

387
26:01.748 --> 26:03.375
Why would he be making a signal like that?

388
26:05.710 --> 26:08.755
And the third thing is this.

389
26:09.339 --> 26:10.382
A ring?

390
26:10.465 --> 26:11.716
I found it on the floor earlier.

391
26:12.425 --> 26:14.594
It's most likely Chief Fukazawa's.

392
26:14.677 --> 26:15.845
Did you not hear me?

393
26:15.929 --> 26:19.599
The Chief always wears this ring,

394
26:19.682 --> 26:21.851
and I found it on the floor.

395
26:27.357 --> 26:28.900
It's strange.

396
26:28.983 --> 26:31.986
An SOS and a wedding ring.

397
26:32.070 --> 26:34.114
Does that mean the chief's wife is in danger?

398
26:36.574 --> 26:37.617
Maybe.

399
26:46.793 --> 26:48.628
TEN MINUTES EARLIER

400
26:58.430 --> 26:59.681
UNKNOWN CALLER

401
27:02.809 --> 27:04.060
Mayumi?

402
27:09.315 --> 27:10.942
WE HAVE YOUR WIFE IN OUR SIGHTS RIGHT NOW

403
27:11.025 --> 27:13.153
DO WHAT WE SAY IF YOU DON'T WANT HER TO BE KILLED

404
27:14.612 --> 27:16.823
-Welcome home. -Thank you very much.

405
27:20.076 --> 27:22.620
THE VULDINIA FLIGHT SHOULD HAVE ARRIVED AT YOUR GATE

406
27:22.704 --> 27:25.290
LET EVERY PASSENGER ENTER THE COUNTRY BY 2:00 P.M.

407
27:35.258 --> 27:36.384
PUT THE RECEIVER DOWN

408
27:36.468 --> 27:38.595
WE CAN SEE WHAT YOU'RE DOING

409
27:38.678 --> 27:39.929
DON'T DO ANYTHING UNNECESSARY

410
27:46.144 --> 27:47.353
Dad!

411
27:51.649 --> 27:52.859
CLOSE THE BLINDS

412
27:52.942 --> 27:53.985
IF YOU RESIST, YOUR WIFE DIES

413
28:11.252 --> 28:12.587
SIT DOWN

414
28:12.670 --> 28:14.797
PUT YOUR PHONE ON THE DESK

415
28:14.881 --> 28:16.758
KEEP BOTH HANDS WHERE WE CAN SEE THEM

416
28:44.911 --> 28:46.287
Let them all in?

417
28:46.371 --> 28:47.205
GATE 24 - SECONDARY ROOM

418
28:47.789 --> 28:50.959
I can't let passengers with problems through.

419
28:53.628 --> 28:55.004
Emergency alert.

420
28:55.088 --> 28:58.299
An explosion has been confirmed in the north lobby.

421
28:58.383 --> 29:02.345
The cause is a power bank catching fire. No injuries.

422
29:10.270 --> 29:11.145
THAT WAS A WARNING

423
29:11.229 --> 29:12.814
LET EVERYONE INTO THE COUNTRY

424
29:12.897 --> 29:14.482
27 MORE MINUTES

425
29:17.026 --> 29:18.903
UNKNOWN CALLER

426
29:26.536 --> 29:27.495
Hayami.

427
29:29.038 --> 29:31.416
Let that passenger through.

428
29:32.667 --> 29:34.586
Forget the inspection.

429
29:35.587 --> 29:37.130
Let him enter the country.

430
29:41.384 --> 29:42.635
THAT'S BETTER

431
29:42.719 --> 29:45.013
NOW SIT QUIETLY

432
30:25.011 --> 30:26.804
I'm almost at the arrival lobby.

433
30:27.347 --> 30:28.973
Your luggage is fine.

434
30:29.057 --> 30:30.725
Please take your passport.

435
30:31.976 --> 30:33.603
I found his wife.

436
30:34.145 --> 30:36.439
Keep watching her.

437
30:36.522 --> 30:38.566
The chief can't hear this line.

438
30:38.650 --> 30:39.817
Okay.

439
30:40.401 --> 30:42.654
-Chief. -What are you doing?

440
30:43.363 --> 30:45.448
Hurry up and let Krone through.

441
30:46.282 --> 30:48.409
Yes, sir. However,

442
30:48.493 --> 30:49.786
we'll process the passengers

443
30:49.869 --> 30:52.956
waiting in line before Mr. Krone.

444
30:55.083 --> 30:56.834
Understood.

445
30:56.918 --> 30:58.294
Just hurry.

446
30:59.170 --> 31:00.004
Yes, sir.

447
31:10.139 --> 31:12.016
-I'll take over. -Thank you.

448
31:14.352 --> 31:17.605
I think the chief is being monitored by someone.

449
31:18.189 --> 31:19.857
-Over here. -By who?

450
31:19.941 --> 31:22.652
Passengers, airport staff…

451
31:23.236 --> 31:25.697
Is there anyone else who could have been here?

452
31:28.866 --> 31:30.952
The AC repairmen yesterday.

453
31:31.995 --> 31:34.372
If they planted something, then…

454
31:46.217 --> 31:47.677
I'll check with security.

455
31:49.095 --> 31:50.972
Jin, can you come with me?

456
31:51.055 --> 31:52.015
Yes.

457
31:57.603 --> 31:59.689
-Over here. -But who would do this, and why?

458
31:59.772 --> 32:03.067
It may be connected to the president's visit to Japan.

459
32:03.151 --> 32:04.027
Welcome home.

460
32:05.278 --> 32:06.988
He said to let all passengers through.

461
32:07.071 --> 32:10.158
And we know that the terrorist leader is coming.

462
32:10.241 --> 32:12.869
Is this to get the leader into the country?

463
32:23.129 --> 32:25.173
Can we check Shirosaki's belongings?

464
32:25.256 --> 32:27.133
I'll contact Iuchi.

465
32:27.216 --> 32:28.760
Let's switch back to the normal line.

466
32:28.843 --> 32:30.261
Contact me if something comes up.

467
32:30.970 --> 32:31.929
Over here.

468
32:44.984 --> 32:46.360
UNKNOWN CALLER: NEW MESSAGE

469
32:46.444 --> 32:48.738
HURRY AND LET EVERYONE INTO THE COUNTRY

470
32:48.821 --> 32:50.573
DON'T HOLD UP THE PASSENGERS

471
32:50.656 --> 32:52.366
TEN MORE MINUTES

472
32:52.450 --> 32:55.411
WORK DETAILS

473
33:10.802 --> 33:13.179
Hayami, Mori, that's enough.

474
33:13.763 --> 33:14.847
Thank you.

475
33:15.473 --> 33:17.475
Let the passengers in the other room through.

476
33:17.558 --> 33:18.810
This way.

477
33:29.278 --> 33:31.864
Chief, sorry to keep you waiting.

478
33:31.948 --> 33:32.949
Hayami.

479
33:33.032 --> 33:36.035
Let Krone into the country.

480
33:36.119 --> 33:40.289
This is an order from the Chief Hearing Officer.

481
33:42.166 --> 33:43.292
Understood.

482
33:43.376 --> 33:44.877
Immigration will let him through.

483
33:45.419 --> 33:48.548
However, the customs inspection isn't finished yet.

484
33:49.132 --> 33:51.676
Please wait a little longer until the inspection is complete.

485
34:05.398 --> 34:06.399
Here.

486
34:10.903 --> 34:12.155
Mori.

487
34:16.868 --> 34:20.246
I'm still waiting for the seed inspection to be completed.

488
34:30.047 --> 34:31.174
Okay.

489
34:32.133 --> 34:32.967
Take care of it.

490
34:33.801 --> 34:34.760
Yes, sir.

491
34:49.108 --> 34:50.067
‎INTERNATIONAL DEPARTURES LOBBY

492
34:50.151 --> 34:52.486
This is the footage the security room sent us.

493
34:55.323 --> 34:56.574
These two.

494
34:57.283 --> 34:59.952
But we can't see their faces clearly.

495
35:01.370 --> 35:02.371
Did you find anything?

496
35:02.455 --> 35:04.207
Counselor? Huh? What about the questioning?

497
35:04.290 --> 35:05.291
Don't worry.

498
35:05.374 --> 35:06.792
Public Security's investigation

499
35:06.876 --> 35:09.879
confirmed there is no connection between the counselor and Wings of the People.

500
35:09.962 --> 35:12.256
Really? Thank goodness!

501
35:12.340 --> 35:13.883
So, what's the situation?

502
35:14.967 --> 35:18.554
As I told you, yesterday's air-conditioner repairmen appear to be suspicious,

503
35:18.638 --> 35:19.472
but their faces…

504
35:19.555 --> 35:22.892
Then our only choice is to identify them in person, right?

505
35:22.975 --> 35:25.436
-In person? -Who actually saw these two?

506
35:25.519 --> 35:28.606
I did. Okay, I'll search for his wife.

507
35:28.689 --> 35:29.607
Let's go.

508
35:30.691 --> 35:34.570
Wait! You only saw their faces in passing,

509
35:34.654 --> 35:36.781
yet you still remember them?

510
35:36.864 --> 35:37.782
Yes.

511
35:38.950 --> 35:41.786
Identifying people is what Immigration does.

512
35:42.453 --> 35:43.287
-Let's go. -Yes!

513
35:47.500 --> 35:49.335
They're reliable people.

514
35:50.378 --> 35:51.879
That's Gate 24.

515
35:54.632 --> 35:56.467
You need to check inside our luggage?

516
35:56.550 --> 35:58.678
There may be seeds inside,

517
35:58.761 --> 36:00.888
so we'd like to check it just to be safe.

518
36:02.223 --> 36:03.182
Yours too, Noa.

519
36:05.017 --> 36:05.851
Go ahead.

520
36:06.811 --> 36:07.812
Excuse me.

521
36:11.315 --> 36:14.402
Hey, Tsumugi, your mom is waiting for you, right?

522
36:14.485 --> 36:15.486
Is it okay?

523
36:16.696 --> 36:18.698
She might be worried.

524
36:20.032 --> 36:22.702
Maybe we don't need that present anymore?

525
36:23.953 --> 36:27.123
But you went to the trouble of getting it for me.

526
36:33.129 --> 36:34.297
Mori.

527
36:36.841 --> 36:39.010
These are Kazuo Shirosaki's belongings.

528
36:39.802 --> 36:40.678
Thank you very much.

529
36:43.848 --> 36:47.143
But are you really sure the Chief's wife is…

530
36:56.027 --> 36:57.486
That's Shirosaki's family.

531
37:04.327 --> 37:08.748
I think they were killed in the Astorian bombing.

532
37:12.335 --> 37:13.627
Oh my.

533
37:27.683 --> 37:28.809
Search all you want.

534
37:29.894 --> 37:33.272
In the end, you'll have to let me in anyway.

535
37:57.254 --> 37:58.798
IT'S TIME

536
37:58.881 --> 38:00.716
DON'T MAKE US WAIT ANY LONGER

537
38:00.800 --> 38:02.385
LET EVERYONE INTO THE COUNTRY NOW

538
38:13.938 --> 38:15.189
That's far enough.

539
38:17.817 --> 38:18.734
Thank you.

540
38:21.278 --> 38:23.322
Finish the inspection.

541
38:40.464 --> 38:42.091
The inspection results are in.

542
38:42.758 --> 38:45.344
These seeds pose no problem under plant quarantine regulations.

543
38:45.928 --> 38:47.513
You can take them with you.

544
38:48.180 --> 38:49.682
Really?

545
38:49.765 --> 38:52.143
-That's great, Tsumugi. -Yes!

546
39:05.239 --> 39:06.866
Time's up, huh?

547
39:16.792 --> 39:18.169
I'm going to check something.

548
39:45.362 --> 39:46.447
Well then.

549
39:48.240 --> 39:49.408
Let me through.

550
39:59.001 --> 40:00.169
Here you are.

551
40:01.295 --> 40:03.214
-Please wait here. -Okay.

552
40:08.886 --> 40:10.429
-Noa, this way. -Okay.

553
40:14.642 --> 40:16.143
Damn it!

554
40:19.980 --> 40:23.692
Chief Fukazawa, we've apprehended the suspect.

555
40:24.860 --> 40:26.237
Your wife

556
40:26.779 --> 40:28.155
is safe.

557
40:33.827 --> 40:36.872
I'm so sorry for the trouble.

558
40:46.298 --> 40:47.466
But…

559
40:49.969 --> 40:51.804
Sorry to keep you waiting, Tsumugi.

560
40:52.972 --> 40:55.057
Wait! Please, let go!

561
40:55.140 --> 40:57.226
We've got some questions for you.

562
40:57.309 --> 40:59.103
-Don't struggle! -You're coming with us.

563
41:00.896 --> 41:02.064
‎Let go of me!

564
41:02.147 --> 41:04.108
-Take him away. -I said let go of me!

565
41:08.445 --> 41:09.738
Let's go, Tsumugi.

566
41:10.489 --> 41:13.158
Wait a minute, Noa.

567
41:15.828 --> 41:16.912
Come on.

568
41:16.996 --> 41:18.872
-Hey, wait… -Noa Shirosaki.

569
41:27.006 --> 41:31.510
That blue cloth was in this photograph.

570
41:34.597 --> 41:37.057
This is a photograph of Kazuo Shirosaki's family.

571
41:38.183 --> 41:43.480
The scarf his wife is wearing is the same color and pattern as that cloth, isn't it?

572
41:49.194 --> 41:51.572
Well, that's just a coincidence, right?

573
41:52.906 --> 41:55.743
We looked into Kazuo Shirosaki's family.

574
41:56.577 --> 41:57.786
Noa Shirosaki.

575
41:58.912 --> 42:00.289
This is you, isn't it?

576
42:00.956 --> 42:04.001
There is a record of you leaving Japan four years ago.

577
42:06.253 --> 42:10.507
You moved from Japan to Astoria with your family,

578
42:10.591 --> 42:14.094
and your mother died in a bombing there.

579
42:15.220 --> 42:19.433
After that, you joined Wings of the People, with your father.

580
42:23.270 --> 42:24.104
Noa?

581
42:26.357 --> 42:27.816
You've got the wrong person.

582
42:28.484 --> 42:30.527
I'm Noa Madsen.

583
42:31.153 --> 42:34.907
I don't know anything about Wings of the People.

584
42:35.908 --> 42:37.159
Iuchi.

585
42:38.118 --> 42:40.829
Apparently, the guys going after Fukazawa's wife

586
42:40.913 --> 42:44.291
were taking orders from someone acting as their leader.

587
42:45.459 --> 42:48.170
I'm going to give that leader a call now.

588
42:57.888 --> 42:58.847
‎MISSED CALL

589
43:00.641 --> 43:05.270
You are the leader of Wings of the People, aren't you?

590
43:09.608 --> 43:10.484
Noa?

591
43:14.446 --> 43:16.573
That door won't open.

592
43:19.201 --> 43:20.953
Don't run!

593
43:23.622 --> 43:24.790
Stop resisting!

594
43:28.127 --> 43:30.421
Your luggage was strange.

595
43:31.380 --> 43:32.965
Even though the contents were almost identical,

596
43:33.716 --> 43:36.677
Tsumugi's was heavier.

597
43:41.598 --> 43:44.685
-Don't touch it! -Excuse me.

598
44:05.414 --> 44:06.373
‎Gems?

599
44:07.499 --> 44:08.792
This is…

600
44:08.876 --> 44:11.670
Funding for Wings of the People.

601
44:14.882 --> 44:16.717
If these had been in your luggage, Noa,

602
44:17.301 --> 44:19.970
you might have been stopped at immigration.

603
44:20.679 --> 44:21.805
But

604
44:21.889 --> 44:25.476
if they were in the luggage of the daughter of the Chief Hearing Officer,

605
44:25.559 --> 44:27.478
a Japanese citizen, they'd never be stopped.

606
44:29.855 --> 44:33.066
So you had Tsumugi carry them for you. Isn't that right?

607
44:34.359 --> 44:35.194
And

608
44:35.277 --> 44:38.864
you thought you and your associates might not be able to enter the country,

609
44:39.406 --> 44:41.325
so you threatened Chief Fukazawa.

610
44:45.704 --> 44:47.372
How much is all this worth?

611
44:55.297 --> 44:56.215
Don't!

612
44:56.298 --> 44:57.591
Let go!

613
44:58.175 --> 44:59.927
-You can't! -Let go!

614
45:00.010 --> 45:01.678
You can't!

615
45:01.762 --> 45:04.389
My mother was killed by the Roden administration.

616
45:04.473 --> 45:07.059
I was going to avenge her with my father.

617
45:07.142 --> 45:09.019
But then my father too…

618
45:09.102 --> 45:10.604
He's alive!

619
45:10.687 --> 45:13.690
Shirosaki is alive!

620
45:14.191 --> 45:16.193
He's in the hospital. Your dad is alive.

621
45:17.194 --> 45:18.028
You can't!

622
45:18.779 --> 45:20.113
You can't die!

623
45:23.492 --> 45:26.036
Stop! You can't!

624
45:26.995 --> 45:28.497
You can't die…

625
45:29.873 --> 45:30.707
You can't…

626
45:32.334 --> 45:34.127
You can't die!

627
45:35.587 --> 45:37.089
You can't!

628
45:38.632 --> 45:41.552
Mori. It's okay now.

629
45:42.177 --> 45:44.221
This time, we stopped it.

630
45:57.109 --> 45:58.402
Can you stand?

631
46:26.179 --> 46:28.015
RESIGNATION

632
46:30.976 --> 46:32.019
Fukazawa.

633
46:32.102 --> 46:36.106
Whatever the reason, I compromised the inspection process.

634
46:36.189 --> 46:38.108
I'm unfit to be an inspector.

635
46:39.318 --> 46:40.444
But…

636
46:42.112 --> 46:44.948
I'm not worried about Gate 24.

637
46:47.367 --> 46:51.413
It's full of people I can rely on.

638
46:56.460 --> 46:59.796
I really did…

639
47:02.132 --> 47:03.300
love that team.

640
47:06.928 --> 47:07.804
Yes.

641
47:09.014 --> 47:10.223
Me too.

642
47:12.267 --> 47:16.813
Last night, thanks to all of your help,

643
47:17.481 --> 47:20.567
we found the domestic base of Wings of the People.

644
47:21.693 --> 47:24.237
Explosives were being manufactured at that hideout.

645
47:24.321 --> 47:26.323
It looks like they were planning to carry out

646
47:26.406 --> 47:28.825
an assassination during President Roden's visit to Japan.

647
47:28.909 --> 47:31.662
Then if we hadn't stopped Noa and the others there…

648
47:31.745 --> 47:36.375
In the worst-case scenario, it could have turned into a suicide bombing.

649
47:36.458 --> 47:37.501
Glad it didn't happen.

650
47:38.126 --> 47:42.631
Honestly, your Gate 24 never stops getting into trouble.

651
47:42.714 --> 47:44.216
I'm very sorry.

652
47:44.299 --> 47:45.175
No.

653
47:45.759 --> 47:48.220
This time, you all did well.

654
47:51.932 --> 47:55.602
This gate might be the very reason they were stopped.

655
47:57.229 --> 47:58.980
We got praised by the Airport Director.

656
47:59.064 --> 48:01.316
I didn't think that was possible.

657
49:01.793 --> 49:03.920
Like I said, don't say it like it's an afterthought.

658
49:11.678 --> 49:12.929
Hayami, this is…

659
49:19.561 --> 49:22.147
Creatine, as declared.

660
49:22.689 --> 49:25.066
Iron, as declared.

661
49:25.984 --> 49:26.943
Melatonin too.

662
49:29.404 --> 49:31.698
Everything is within the permitted quantities this time.

663
49:31.782 --> 49:34.409
Right? I studied up because of you.

664
49:35.368 --> 49:37.120
-Thank you very much. -Me too.

665
49:37.704 --> 49:40.457
Knowing you check everything so carefully, I can rest easy at night.

666
49:41.041 --> 49:42.000
Yes!

667
49:52.844 --> 49:54.888
Welcome to Japan.

668
49:57.557 --> 49:58.975
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
